From: fllama (not yet upstream)
Subject: ggml-metal : do not free the Metal devices at exit

ggml_metal_device_get keeps the devices in a static vector. At exit its
destructor calls ggml_metal_device_free, which asserts that the residency
set collection is empty: no Metal buffer may still exist. An app that holds
a loaded model when it exits (macOS calls exit() on quit) aborts there with
GGML_ASSERT([rsets->data count] == 0). llama.cpp's own tools free their
models before exit; an app that embeds llama.cpp cannot always do that. The
vector is now never destroyed, so the OS reclaims the devices with the
process. Upstream master 9581154a2 (2026-11-17) has the same code. Drop this
patch when llama.cpp fixes it.
---
diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device.cpp
index 0d18a5f0..c62083e4 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device.cpp
@@ -20,11 +20,13 @@ struct ggml_metal_device_deleter {
 typedef std::unique_ptr<ggml_metal_device, ggml_metal_device_deleter> ggml_metal_device_ptr;
 
 ggml_metal_device_t ggml_metal_device_get(int device, int n_devices) {
-    static std::vector<ggml_metal_device_ptr> devs;
+    // never destroyed: at exit, a model the app still holds has Metal buffers,
+    // and ggml_metal_device_free asserts that there are none
+    static auto * devs = new std::vector<ggml_metal_device_ptr>();
 
-    devs.emplace_back(ggml_metal_device_init(device, n_devices));
+    devs->emplace_back(ggml_metal_device_init(device, n_devices));
 
-    return devs.back().get();
+    return devs->back().get();
 }
 
 struct ggml_metal_pipelines {
